===persian===

تو را دوباره نگاه کردم...
دوباره مژگان را...
درون برکهٔ مهتاب شستشو دادم...
تو را نگاه کردم...
و پلک‌های تَرَم را...
در آبِ چشمهٔ دیدن...
چنان صفا دادم... که...
رنگ‌های صدایت را...
بگوش می‌دیدم...
و با نگاه ترم... بر لبانِ بیدارت....
هزار گفتهٔ گرمِ خموش می‌دیدم...
لبانِ تو می‌دید...
و چشم‌های تو در گوشه‌های بیداری...
ترانه‌ای می‌خواند...
کلام سبزِ ترِ عاشقانه‌ای می‌خواند...
۱۳۷۰/۱/۱۳

===machine===

I looked at you again...
Again I washed my lashes...
in the pool of the moonlight...
I looked at you...
and my wet eyelids...
in the water of the spring of seeing...
I rinsed so clear... that...
the colours of your voice...
I saw with my ear...
and with my wet gaze... on your waking lips....
I saw a thousand warm silent sayings...
Your lips were seeing...
and your eyes in the corners of wakefulness...
were singing a song...
were singing a green wet word of love...
1370/1/13

===lantern===

I looked at you again...
Again I washed my lashes
in the pool of the moonlight...
I looked at you,
and rinsed my wet eyelids
in the water of the spring of seeing
until they ran so clear
that I saw the colours of your voice
with my ear...
and with that wet looking, on your waking lips,
I saw a thousand warm silent sayings...
Your lips were seeing...
and your eyes, in the corners of being awake,
were singing a song —
were singing a green wet word of love...

1370/1/13

===translation===

===footnotes===

*I saw the colours of your voice with my ear* is not a slip. The senses swap places all
through this pair of poems — the eyes sing, the lips see, the ears do the looking — and the poem
on the facing page ends with ears that are still seeing.
